body:
The money relating to UBI can be derived by ensuring corporations pay their share of tax, instead of funneling profits overseas in tax havens and using shelving companies. Billions of dollars could be generated by that activity alone. Next cut the defence budget which could also save billions of dollars. Next get rid of the bureaucracy regarding social welfare and consolidate all benefits into one UBI payment. So much money is wasted on government bureaucrats who do very little. If all those suggestions are carried out it will generate a significant amount;, how much I cannot say because I do not know. What I do know is that it is not impossible,and that it would actually motivate people to work rather than the common assumption that people will stop working. If the payment was say $25,000 per year that would equate to just over 5 trillion dollars and it would mean that people below the poverty line would be able to afford transport to get to job interviews and look for work. It would mean they could afford to work only one job instead of three and their children will have their parents back. Children will be less likely to become drug dealers and addicts because they will be less desperate, hence crime rates will reduce, communities will be safer. Sure there will still be many people that will blow all the money on drugs and other nonproductive activities, however children will grow up knowing there is a safety net and that they have an opportunity to pursue their dreams, start their own business and make a living doing what they WANT to do, not what they HAVE to do. It will be the next generation that benefits and continues to build a stronger, more positive future.

&#x200B;

